    "category": "IM Cardio",
    "q": "Why is a VSD not cyanotic at birth per p6?",
    "a": "Only years later does high pulmonary blood flow cause pulmonary hypertension, then RVH and reversal R to L (Eisenmenger), making the patient cyanotic.",
